\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* King¦155591 David¦155592 had¦155594 become very old¦155593, and¦155591 \add ≈he couldn't keep warm¦155599 even when covered¦155596 with¦155597 blankets\add*,
\v 2 \add ≈so\add* his¦155604 servants¦155604 \add ≈suggested\add*, “\add ≈Allow us search¦155605 for¦155606 a young¦155608 woman¦155608 who can wait on¦155618 you and take care of your¦155618 needs¦155605. She¦155617 can sleep beside you and keep our\add* master¦155606, the¦155621 king¦155621, warm¦155619.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦155623\add* they¦155623 searched¦155623 \add ≈throughout\add* Yisrael¦155628 and found¦155629 a beautiful¦155625 young¦155624 woman¦155624 called Avishag¦155632 (a Shunammite¦155633) and brought¦155634 her¦155635 to¦155636 the king¦155636.
\v 4 \add *She\add* was incredibly beautiful¦155639 and¦155638 she¦155646 \add ≈took care of\add* the king, but¦155638 \add *he¦155649\add* didn't¦155648 \add ≈have sexual¦155649 relations\add* with her¦155649.
