\v 5 Then¦155651 \add David and\add* Haggit's¦155654 son¦155652 Adoniyah \add ≈promoted himself¦155655\add* saying¦155656, “I¦155657, myself, will reign.” He¦155659 \add ≈acquired\add* a chariot¦155661 and horsemen¦155662 and fifty¦155663 men who ran¦155665 \add ≈along in front¦155666\add*.\x + \xo 1:5: \xt 2Sam 3:4.\x*
\v 6 \add @Haggit\add* had given birth to him after¦155686 Avshalom. He¦155679 was¦155680 \add ≈a good-looker\add*, \add but\add* his¦155672 father¦155671 \add ≈had never disciplined\add* him \add or ever\add* asked, “Why did you¦155676 do that?”
\v 7 \add ≈He had spoken\add* with¦155691 Tseruyah's¦155695 son¦155693 Yoav¦155692 and the¦155698 priest¦155698 Evyatar and they¦155689 had \add both\add* \add ≈agreed to support¦155699\add* \add *him\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈But¦155703\add* the priest¦155704 Tsadok and Yehoyada's¦155708 son¦155706 Benayah¦155705, the prophet¦155710 Natan¦155709, Shimei¦155711 and Rei¦155712, and \add ≈David's¦155715 top warriors\add* were¦155717 \add all\add* \add ≈against\add* Adoniyah¦155720.
