\v 11 Then¦155765 Natan¦155766 \add ≈asked\add* Shelomoh's¦155774 mother¦155772 Batsheva, “Haven't you¦155777 heard¦155777 that¦155778 Haggit's¦155783 son¦155781 Adoniyah¦155780 \add ≈has¦155779 made himself king¦155779\add*, and¦155784 our¦155784 master¦155784 David¦155785 doesn't \add even\add* \add ≈realise\add*?\x + \xo 1:11: \xt 2Sam 12:24.\x*
\v 12 \add ≈So¦155789\add* please¦155792 let¦155791 me¦155791 advise you now¦155789 \add ≈so that you can save¦155794 your own life and¦155789 that of your son¦155801 Shelomoh¦155802\add* \add !(Solomon¦155802)\add*.
\v 13 Go¦155805 and \add ≈ask\add* King¦155809 David¦155810, ‘My¦155816 master¦155816 the¦155817 king, didn't¦155813 you¦155818 promise your female¦155819 servant, saying, “Surely your son¦155824 Shelomoh¦155823 will reign¦155825 after¦155826 me¦155826, and he will sit¦155828 on¦155829 my¦155831 throne¦155831?” \add ≈So why¦155832 has¦155833 Adoniyah¦155834 become¦155833 king\add*?’
\v 14 Then¦155844 while you're still¦155838 there¦155840 talking¦155839 to the king¦155843, I'll¦155845 come¦155845 in behind you and \add ≈confirm¦155847 what you said\add*.”
