\v 17 “My¦155887 master¦155884,” she¦155882 \add ≈replied\add*, “you yourself \add ≈promised\add* to your female servant¦155889 \add ≈in¦155887 front of\add* your god¦155888 Yahweh¦155884 that your son¦155893 Shelomoh¦155892 \add ≈would be the one to reign¦155894 after¦155895 you and¦155882 sit¦155897 on¦155887 your\add* throne¦155900.
\v 18 \add ≈But¦155902\add* now, listen, Adoniyah¦155904 \add ≈has¦155905 become¦155905 king\add* \add instead\add*, and¦155902 you¦155910 \add ≈haven't even been told about it\add*.
\v 19 He's¦155912 sacrificing¦155912 \add ≈many\add* oxen and calves and sheep¦155916, and he¦155918 invited¦155931 the priest¦155924 Evyatar¦155923, and Yoav¦155925 the commander¦155926 of¦155926 the army¦155927, and all your sons¦155921 \add ≈except for\add* your servant¦155929 Shelomoh¦155928.
