\v 22 \add ≈Just\add* then¦155967, while she¦155968 was¦155969 still¦155968 talking¦155969 with¦155970 the king¦155972, the prophet¦155974 Natan¦155973 \add ≈appeared\add*
\v 23 and \add ≈his arrival\add* was announced to the king. He¦155981 went¦155983 \add ≈into the room and knelt in¦155984 front¦155984 of¦155984 the king and bowed¦155986 his face¦155990\add* to the floor.
\v 24 Then¦155993 \add *he¦155993\add* \add ≈asked\add*, “My¦155994 master¦155995 the¦155996 king¦155996, \add ≈did you announce that Adoniyah¦155999 will reign¦156000 after¦156001 you and¦155993 sit¦156003 on¦156004 your\add* throne¦156006?
\v 25 \add I ask\add* because¦156008 today he sacrificed¦156012 plenty of oxen and calves and sheep¦156016. He'd \add ≈invited\add* all your sons¦156021 and army¦156024 commanders¦156023, and Evyatar the¦156026 priest¦156026. They're \add all\add* eating¦156028 and drinking¦156029 with him¦156030 and saying¦156031, ‘\add ≈Long live¦156032\add* King¦156022 Adoniyah¦156034!’
\v 26 But¦156036 as for me¦156036, I'm¦156037 \em your\em* servant, and¦156036 \add ≈nor did he invite¦156049\add* Tsadok¦156040 the priest¦156041 or Yehoyada's¦156045 son¦156043 Benayah¦156042, or Shelomoh¦156046 your servant.
\v 27 Did¦156060 my master the king \add ≈organise that¦156057 without telling\add* your¦156062 servants¦156062 who¦156064 will¦156065 sit¦156065 on¦156066 the throne¦156068 of¦156068 my master the king after¦156072 him¦156072?”
\rem /s1 David Makes Solomon King; The Accession of Solomon
\p
\v 28 Then King¦156076 David¦156077 said¦156078, “Call Batsheva \add back in\add*.” \add ≈So\add* she¦156088 came¦156085 \add back\add* into the¦156089 king's¦156087 \add room\add* and¦156088 stood¦156088 in front¦156086 of¦156089 \add *him\add*.
\v 29 Then¦156092 the king¦156093 \add ≈promised\add*, “As¦156101 Yahweh¦156097 lives \add ≈and¦156094 has¦156100 rescued me from¦156104 every danger\add*,
\v 30 I promise you \add in front of\add* Yisrael's¦156114 god¦156113 Yahweh¦156112 that¦156132 your¦156119 son¦156119 Shelomoh¦156118 will reign¦156120 after¦156121 me¦156121 and¦156122 will sit¦156123 on¦156112 my throne¦156126 in my place¦156127. \add ≈I'll¦156130 put it in action today\add*.”
\p
\v 31 Batsheva \add ≈knelt down and bowed¦156134 her face¦156138 to¦156141 the floor\add* and said¦156142, “May my master¦156144, the king¦156145 David¦156146 live¦156143 \add ≈forever\add*.”
\p
\v 32 Then King¦156152 David¦156153 \add ≈called out\add*, “\add ≈Summon¦156154\add* Tsadok¦156157 the priest¦156158 for me¦156156, and Natan¦156159 the prophet¦156160, and Yehoyada's¦156164 son¦156162 Benayah¦156161.” \add ≈So\add* they¦156165 came¦156165 \add ≈into the king's¦156167 room\add*.
\v 33 “Take¦156172 some of \add *my\add* servants¦156176,” the king¦156170 \add ≈instructed\add* them¦156171. “and put my son¦156182 Shelomoh¦156181 on¦156183 my mule¦156185 and lead him¦156190 to¦156191 the Gihon¦156193 \add Spring\add*.
\v 34 Then \add you two,\add* Tsadok¦156198 and Natan¦156200, must¦156195 anoint¦156195 him¦156196 there¦156197 as king¦156202 over¦156203 Yisrael¦156205. Then blow the¦156201 horn¦156207 and \add ≈shout\add*, ‘Let King¦156202 Shelomoh¦156211 live¦156209!’
\v 35 Then \add ≈follow him¦156214 back here where he must¦156213\add* come¦156215 and sit¦156216 on¦156217 my throne¦156219. Then he'll¦156215 reign¦156221 in¦156222 my place¦156222 as ruler¦156226 of¦156222 Yisrael¦156229 and Yehudah¦156232.”
\p
\v 36 “\add ≈Certainly\add*,” Benayah¦156235 replied. “Just as Yahweh¦156249, the god¦156248 of my¦156249 master¦156249 the king¦156250 has instructed.
\v 37 Just¦156254 as¦156252 Yahweh¦156257 has¦156253 been¦156253 with my master the king, so¦156259 may he¦156260 be with Shelomoh¦156264. And¦156265 may \add ≈his¦156268 rule be\add* \add even\add* greater¦156265 than¦156269 \add *that\add* of¦156269 my master, the king David¦156272.”
\p
\v 38 \add ≈So¦156274\add* Tsadok¦156275 the priest¦156276 and Natan¦156277 the prophet¦156278 and Yehoyada's¦156282 son¦156280 Benayah¦156279 and the \add ≈kings bodyguards\add* went and put Shelomoh¦156288 on¦156289 the king's mule, and took him¦156295 to¦156296 Gihon¦156298.
\v 39 Tsadok¦156301 the priest¦156302 took¦156300 the horn of¦156305 oil¦156306 from¦156307 the sacred tent¦156309 and anointed¦156310 Shelomoh \add with it\add*, and they¦156316 blew the horn and all¦156317 the people¦156319 \add ≈shouted\add*, “Let King¦156321 Shelomoh live¦156320!”
\v 40 Then¦156324 all¦156325 the people \add ≈followed\add* him¦156328 \add back\add* uphill \add to the city\add*, and the people were playing¦156330 flutes¦156330 and were \add ≈so exuberant in¦156331 their¦156337 celebrations that the ground shook¦156335 with¦156331 the noise¦156337\add*.
\p
\v 41 \add ≈When¦156339\add* Adoniyah¦156340 and all \add ≈his invited¦156343 guests¦156343\add* had¦156347 finished¦156347 eating¦156348, they heard the noise, and Yoav¦156350 heard the sound¦156353 of the horn¦156354 and \add ≈asked\add*, “\add ≈What's all that commotion in\add* the city¦156359?”
\v 42 He¦156362 was¦156363 still speaking¦156363 when Yonatan¦156365 the son¦156366 of¦156366 Evyatar the priest¦156369 \add suddenly turned up\add*, and Adoniyah¦156372 \add ≈called\add* \add >him\add*, “Come¦156373 \add over here\add* because¦156374 you're a \add ≈good fellow\add* and you'll bring good news¦156379.”
\p
\v 43 “\add Actually, no,\add*” Yonatan¦156382 answered¦156381. “Our¦156386 master¦156386 the¦156387 king David¦156389 has¦156390 \add just\add* made¦156390 Shelomoh¦156393 \add ≈king\add*.
\v 44 The¦156398 king sent¦156395 Tsadok¦156401 the priest¦156402 and Natan¦156405 the prophet¦156406 and Yehoyada's¦156410 son¦156408 Benayah¦156407 and the \add ≈king's bodyguards\add*, and they¦156413 placed \add @Shelomoh\add* on¦156415 the king's mule.
\v 45 Then¦156419 Tsadok¦156421 and Natan¦156423 anointed¦156419 him as king¦156425 at¦156426 Gihon¦156426. \add Now\add* they've¦156419 \add ≈gone¦156427 back\add* from there¦156428 \add ≈cheering\add* \add all the way\add*, and the \add whole\add* city¦156431 is \add happily\add* \add ≈celebrating\add*. That's the noise¦156433 that¦156434 you're all hearing¦156435.
\v 46 \add ≈What's more\add*, Shelomoh's¦156439 sitting¦156438 on¦156440 the¦156441 royal¦156442 throne¦156441 \add right now\add*.
\v 47 \add ≈As well as that\add*, the king's¦156448 servants¦156447 \add ≈went in\add* to¦156449 bless¦156449 our¦156452 master¦156452 the king David¦156454, saying¦156455, ‘May¦156456 God make Shelomoh's¦156462 \add ≈reputation¦156461\add* \add even\add* better than yours, and¦156444 may¦156464 he¦156464 make his \add ≈reign\add* \add even\add* greater¦156464 than yours.’ Then¦156444 the king in his bed¦156473, bowed¦156469 down
\v 48 and said¦156478, ‘Blessed¦156480 be¦156480 Yisrael's¦156483 god¦156482 Yahweh¦156481 who¦156484 has¦156485 \add ≈provided\add* \add a son\add* to sit¦156487 on¦156488 my throne¦156490 today, and \add ≈I've been able to see¦156492 it\add* \add before my death\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 49 Then¦156494 all Adoniyah's¦156500 invited¦156498 guests¦156498 started trembling¦156494, and they all got up¦156495 and \add ≈quietly slipped back to¦156503 their homes\add*.
\v 50 Adoniyah \add himself\add* was¦156506 now afraid¦156506 of what Shelomoh¦156508 would do, \add ≈so\add* he went¦156510 \add to the sacred tent\add* and¦156505 held¦156511 on¦156512 to the horns¦156512 of the altar¦156513.
\v 51 Shelomoh was¦156515 told¦156515, “Listen, Adoniyah¦156519 \add ≈is afraid of the new king because\add* he's¦156526 grabbed¦156526 the horns¦156527 of the altar¦156528 and¦156515 said, ‘Let¦156530 Shelomoh the king promise me as soon as \add ≈possible\add*, that he won't \add ≈execute\add* his¦156541 servant¦156541 with¦156527 the sword¦156542.’ ”
\p
\v 52 “If he \add ≈shows himself as a loyal subject\add*,” Shelomoh¦156545 \add ≈responded¦156544\add*, “\add ≈then he'll be able to keep his head\add*. \add ≈But¦156544\add* if \add ≈he's found¦156559 to be a traitor\add*, then he'll die¦156562.”
\v 53 \add ≈So¦156564\add* King¦156565 Shelomoh sent¦156564 \add for Adoniyah\add*, and they¦156567 brought¦156567 him down from¦156568 beside the altar¦156569. He¦156570 came¦156570 and bowed¦156571 down to¦156572 Shelomoh the king¦156572 and Shelomoh told him, “Go¦156578 \add ≈home¦156579\add*.”
\c 2
\s1 David's final words to Shelomoh
\rem /s1 David's Charge to Solomon; David's Instruction to Solomon; David's Last Instructions to Solomon; David's Final Instructions to Solomon
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈When David¦156585 knew that his death was close, he¦156587 instructed¦156587\add* his son¦156591 Shelomoh¦156590,
\v 2 “I'll soon be \add ≈coming to¦156595 my end, but¦156600\add* \add you must be\add* strong¦156600 and¦156601 \add ≈sensible\add*.
\v 3 You¦156604 \add ≈must¦156604 maintain\add* your¦156610 god¦156610 Yahweh's¦156609 charge¦156607 to walk in his ways¦156612, to keep¦156604 his statutes¦156614, his commands¦156615, his judgements¦156616, and his testimonies¦156617, according¦156618 to what¦156618 is¦156618 written¦156618 in Mosheh's¦156620 instructions¦156614, so¦156621 that you'll¦156604 \add ≈be wise\add* in everything you do¦156627 and everywhere that you turn¦156632,
\v 4 so that Yahweh's¦156637 promise¦156640 to me that he'd keep one of¦156640 my descendants on¦156654 Yisrael's¦156669 throne¦156668, will stand because he gave the condition, ‘If¦156645 your¦156648 descendants will \add ≈obey me and worship me\add* in¦156654 truth with all their \add #hearts¦156657\add* and with all their \add #souls\add*.’
\p
\v 5 “Also¦156671 you're \add ≈aware of\add* what Tseruyah's¦156682 son Yoav¦156679 did to me—what he¦156684 did to two¦156685 of the commanders¦156687 of Yisrael's¦156689 armies¦156688—to Ner's¦156693 son Abner¦156690 and to Yeter's¦156697 son Amasa¦156694. He¦156698 murdered¦156698 them¦156698, \add ≈shedding blood\add* in peace\add -time\add* \add ≈as if it¦156704 was in a war\add*, and \add ≈the blood guilt is on¦156703 him from head to toe\add*.\x + \xo 2:5: a \xt 2Sam 3:27; \xo b \xt 2Sam 20:10.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈So¦156721 use\add* your¦156715 \add own\add* wisdom¦156715, but¦156714 don't¦156716 let \add @Yoav\add* \add ≈get old and¦156716 die peacefully¦156720\add*.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈However,\add* return loyal¦156729 kindness to the sons¦156724 of¦156724 Barzillai¦156725 the Gileadite¦156726, and¦156730 \add ≈invite them to join you¦156727\add* at¦156731 your table¦156732 because¦156733 they \add ≈helped\add* me¦156737 when¦156738 I¦156738 was fleeing¦156738 from¦156739 your brother¦156741 Abshalom¦156740.\x + \xo 2:7: \xt 2Sam 17:27-29.\x*
\p
\v 8 Then there's Gera's¦156748 son¦156746 Shimei¦156745, the Benyamite from¦156752 Bahurim¦156752. He¦156753 cursed¦156754 me \add ≈horribly when I was\add* going to Mahanaim¦156759. Then he went¦156758 down¦156762 to meet¦156763 me at¦156767 the Yordan¦156764, and¦156743 I promised him by Yahweh¦156767 that I wouldn't \add ≈execute\add* him,\x + \xo 2:8: \xt 2Sam 16:5-13; 19:16-23.\x*
\v 9 \add ≈so\add* don't¦156775 leave¦156777 him unpunished¦156777 now. You're a wise¦156780 man¦156779 and¦156774 you'll¦156782 know¦156782 \add ≈how to handle\add* him. \add ≈Although he's old, make sure he has a bloody¦156792 death\add*.
\s1 David's death
