\v 19 \add ≈So¦156936\add* Batsheva¦156937 went¦156936 to King¦156942 Shelomoh¦156943 to speak¦156944 to him¦156946 \add ≈on Adoniyah's¦156949 behalf\add*. The¦156951 king¦156951 rose¦156950 to meet¦156952 her and bowed¦156953 down¦156953 to her. Then¦156936 he sat¦156955 on his throne and he had a throne placed on his right¦156964 for¦156961 his mother¦156961 to sit on.
\v 20 Then¦156966 she¦156966 said¦156966, “I¦156970 have one¦156968 small¦156969 request for you. \add Please\add* \add ≈don't¦156973 say you won't¦156973 do¦156973 it\add*”
\p “\add What's your\add* request, my¦156978 mother¦156984,” the king¦156982 \add ≈responded¦156966\add*, “because¦156985 I \add ≈couldn't refuse you\add*.”
\p
\v 21 “Let Avishag¦156997 the Shunammite¦156998,” she said¦156993, “be given¦156994 to your brother¦157000 Adoniyah¦156999 as a wife.”
\p
\v 22 King¦157004 Shelomoh¦157005 answered¦157003 his mother¦157007, “You're requesting Avishag¦157013 the Shunammite¦157014 for Adoniyah¦157015! \add ≈You might as well\add* request the \add ≈throne\add* for him¦157018, because¦157022 he's my¦157024 brother¦157024 and he's older¦157025 than¦157026 I am! And then¦157003 \add he'll want\add* Evyatar the priest¦157029 and Tseruyah's¦157033 son¦157031 Yoav¦157030!”
\v 23 Then Shelomoh¦157038 promised by¦157039 Yahweh¦157039, “May¦157042 God¦157045 do¦157042 to¦157044 me¦157044 \add ≈whatever he¦157047 wants\add*, unless Adoniyah¦157051 \add ≈pays with¦157039 his¦157049 life¦157049 for¦157044 saying¦157040 that¦157055\add*.
\v 24 And now¦157057 as Yahweh¦157060 \add ≈lives\add*, the one who established¦157062 me and caused me to sit¦157063 on¦157065 the throne¦157067 of my¦157069 father¦157069 David, and who \add ≈promised David's¦157068 descendants to continue reigning\add*, Adoniyah¦157080 will¦157079 certainly be¦157079 put¦157079 to death¦157079 today.”
\p
\v 25 \add ≈So¦157082\add* King¦157083 Shelomoh¦157084 \add ≈instructed\add* Yehoyada's¦157089 son¦157087 Benayah¦157086 and he \add went and\add* struck¦157090 \add @Adoniyah\add* down and he died¦157093.
\s1 Evyatar's banishment and Yoav's death
