\p
\v 26 Then concerning Evyatar the priest¦157097, the king¦157099 told \add >him\add*, “Go¦157101 to¦157102 your¦157104 fields¦157104 at¦157109 Anatot¦157100 because you're \add ≈marked for\add* death¦157107, but¦157096 I¦157112 won't¦157111 \add ≈do it today\add* because you carried¦157115 my master¦157119 Yahweh's¦157120 \add sacred\add* box¦157118 \add ≈ahead of\add* my father David¦157122, and¦157124 because you \add ≈suffered through\add* all¦157126 that¦157110 my father \add ≈suffered\add*.”\x + \xo 2:26: a \xt 2Sam 15:24; \xo b \xt 1Sam 22:20-23.\x*
\v 27 \add That was how\add* Shelomoh¦157133 \add banished\add* Evyatar from¦157137 being¦157137 a priest¦157138 to Yahweh. \add It was done\add* to fulfill¦157140 what Yahweh had¦157146 said at Shiloh¦157151 said about¦157143 \add removing\add* \add ≈Eli's¦157150 descendants\add*.\x + \xo 2:27: \xt 1Sam 2:27-36.\x*
\p
\v 28 \add ≈When\add* the \add ≈news¦157154 of that reached\add* Yoav¦157160, he fled¦157168 to¦157170 Yahweh's¦157173 tent¦157172 and¦157174 held¦157174 onto the horns¦157175 of the altar¦157176, because¦157159 \add *he\add* had \add ≈supported\add* Adoniyah¦157163 (even though he hadn't \add ≈supported\add* Avshalom).
\v 29 \add Someone\add* told¦157178 King¦157179 Shelomoh that¦157181 Yoav¦157183 had¦157182 fled¦157182 to¦157184 Yahweh's¦157187 tent¦157186 and was¦157189 \add there\add* beside¦157189 the altar¦157190, \add ≈so\add* Shelomoh \add ≈instructed\add* Yehoyada's¦157198 son¦157196 Benayah¦157195, “Go \add ≈and strike him¦157203 down\add*.”
\v 30 \add ≈So\add* Benayah¦157206 entered Yahweh's¦157210 tent¦157209 and¦157235 he¦157224 told \add @Yoav¦157234\add*, “The king¦157216 said¦157218 for you to come¦157217 out¦157217.”
\p “No¦157220, I'll¦157223 die¦157223 here¦157222,” he \add ≈replied\add*.
\p \add ≈So\add* Benayah \add ≈went¦157205 back¦157224 to the king and reported both sides of the conversation\add*
\v 31 and the king¦157240 told him, “Just¦157242 do¦157241 \add ≈what he¦157243 said¦157238\add*. \add ≈Kill\add* him and bury¦157247 him, and \add in that way\add* you'll¦157247 remove¦157248 \add ≈the blood guilt from¦157255 me¦157255 and my descendants\add* for the blood that Yoav¦157254 shed¦157253 without¦157251 cause¦157251.
\v 32 Yahweh¦157261 will¦157260 return his blood¦157264 onto his \add own\add* head¦157267, because he attacked two¦157270 men¦157272 more righteous¦157273 and better¦157274 than himself: Ner's¦157287 son Abner¦157284, the commander of Yisrael's¦157291 army, and Yeter's¦157297 son Amasa¦157294, the commander of Yehudah's¦157301 army. He killed¦157276 them with the sword¦157277 and my father¦157278 David¦157279 didn't¦157280 \add ≈have anything to do with it\add*.
\v 33 Their¦157304 shed blood¦157304 will return¦157303 onto Joav's¦157306 head¦157305 and on¦157305 the¦157307 \add #heads\add* of¦157307 his \add ≈descendants forever\add*. But¦157303 for David¦157310 and his \add ≈family\add* and his \add ≈descendants\add* and his throne¦157313, \add ≈Yahweh¦157320 will give\add* peace¦157315 \add ≈forever\add*.”
\p
\v 34 \add ≈So¦157322\add* Yehoyada's¦157326 son¦157324 Benayah¦157323 went and \add ≈struck¦157327\add* \add @Yoav\add* \add at the altar\add* and \add ≈killed¦157330\add* him¦157330. Then¦157322 he was¦157331 buried¦157331 on¦157332 his¦157332 \add property\add* in¦157332 the wilderness¦157333.
\v 35 The king¦157336 \add ≈appointed\add* Benayah¦157339 \add ≈as army¦157346 commander to replace\add* \add @Yoav\add*, and¦157335 \add ≈appointed\add* Tsadok¦157349 as priest¦157350 in place¦157353 of Evyatar.
\s1 Shimei's execution
