\p
\v 1 Shelomoh¦157570 made himself the son-in-law¦157569 of Egypt's¦157575 king¦157574 Far-oh \add ≈by taking¦157576 Far-oh's daughter¦157579 as a wife\add* and bringing¦157582 her¦157582 into the city¦157585 of David¦157586 (\add where she stayed\add* until¦157587 \add ≈the completion of the construction of his¦157592 palace and of Yahweh's¦157596 temple\add*, and the wall¦157599 around¦157601 Yerushalem¦157600).
\v 2 \add ≈However,\add* the¦157604 people¦157604 were¦157605 sacrificing¦157605 \add ≈on¦157606 various hills\add* because¦157607 \add ≈at¦157606 that time¦157615\add*, a \add ≈temple\add* hadn't \add yet\add* been¦157610 built¦157610 for¦157612 Yahweh¦157613.
\v 3 Shelomoh¦157620 \add demonstrated his\add* \add ≈love¦157619 for\add* Yahweh¦157623 by \add ≈obeying the¦157625 instructions¦157625\add* of¦157625 his father¦157627 David¦157626. \add ≈However,\add* he¦157630 would \add offer\add* sacrifices¦157631 and¦157632 burn incense¦157632 \add ≈on¦157625 various hills\add*.
\p
\v 4 \add One time,\add* the king¦157635 went¦157634 to Gibeon¦157636 to sacrifice¦157637 there¦157638, because¦157639 it was¦157641 the \add ≈most popular\add* high¦157641 place¦157641. Shelomoh¦157646 offered¦157644 up a thousand¦157643 burnt¦157644 up \add ≈sacrifices¦157637\add* on¦157647 that¦157649 altar¦157648,
\v 5 and that night¦157658 in Gibeon, Yahweh¦157653 appeared¦157652 to Shelomoh¦157656 in a dream¦157657 and \add ≈asked¦157661\add*, “What¦157662 would you like me to give¦157663 you?”
\p
\v 6 Shelomoh¦157668 \add ≈replied\add*, “You yourself \add ≈showed incredible loyalty to\add* your servant¦157673 David¦157674, my father¦157675, because he walked¦157679 in faithfulness¦157681 and obedience \add ≈in front¦157680 of¦157683 you\add*, and \add ≈did¦157670 what he believed you¦157682 wanted\add*. And you've¦157670 \add ≈maintained this loyalty towards¦157685\add* him and you \add ≈allowed him to have\add* a son¦157697 sitting¦157698 on¦157681 his¦157701 throne¦157701 as¦157702 \add ≈I am today\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈So¦157705\add* now¦157705, Yahweh¦157706 my god¦157707, you yourself have¦157709 caused your¦157712 servant¦157712 to reign in¦157713 place¦157713 of my father¦157715 David¦157714, but¦157705 I'm¦157716 \add ≈still young¦157718—I don't¦157719 really know¦157720 much about¦157707 anything\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈Yet\add* your servant¦157724 is among your chosen¦157728 people—a numerous¦157731 people who can't¦157733 be counted¦157737 because \add ≈there's so many\add* \add of us\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈So¦157740 please\add* give¦157740 your servant¦157741 \add ≈the ability to listen¦157743 to your people and to judge them well\add*—discerning¦157748 between¦157749 good¦157751 and evil¦157752, because¦157753 who's¦157754 able¦157755 to judge your people—\add ≈that's a heavy task\add*.”
\p
\v 10 \add ≈Yahweh¦157766 was¦157763 very pleased that Shelomoh¦157769 had¦157768 requested that\add*
\v 11 and told him, “Because¦157781 you requested that¦157784 and didn't¦157785 request a long life¦157798 or riches for yourself, or requested the¦157798 \add #lives\add* of your¦157799 enemies¦157799, but¦157775 you requested discernment¦157803 for yourself \add ≈when listening and dispensing\add* justice,
\v 12 then I've done¦157807 \add ≈what you requested\add*. Listen, I've given¦157811 you a wise¦157814 and discerning¦157815 \add ≈mind¦157813 unlike anyone who's lived before you or who will¦157825 live in the future\add* after¦157822 you.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦157828\add* I've¦157833 also¦157828 given¦157833 you what you didn't¦157830 request: both¦157835 riches and¦157828 honour¦157840—there'll be \add ≈no other king like¦157845 you for as long as you live\add*,
\v 14 and if¦157852 you'll¦157854 \add ≈obey\add* my statutes¦157857 and commands¦157858 like your father¦157862 David¦157861 did, then¦157852 I'll¦157862 \add also\add* lengthen¦157863 your \add ≈life\add*.”
\p
\v 15 Then Shelomoh¦157870 \add ≈woke up\add*, and wow, it¦157872 had been a dream¦157872, and he went¦157873 \add into\add* Yerushalem¦157874 and stood¦157875 \add ≈in¦157877 front¦157877 of the sacred chest¦157879\add*. Then he offered up burnt¦157884 offerings and made¦157885 peace¦157886 offerings, and he \add ≈held\add* a feast¦157888 for all¦157889 his¦157891 servants¦157891.
\s1 Shelomoh judges a difficult case
\rem /s1 Solomon Judges a Difficult Case; Solomon's Wisdom in Judgment; Solomon Judges Wisely; A Wise Ruling
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 16 \add ≈One day\add* two¦157896 prostitutes¦157898 came¦157895 to¦157899 the¦157901 king¦157901 and¦157902 stood¦157902 \add ≈in front¦157903 of\add* him¦157903,
\v 17 and one of them said¦157905, “Please¦157916, my master¦157909, \add ≈us two women live in the same\add* house, and \add ≈while she was there\add* in the house, I¦157910 gave¦157916 birth¦157916 \add to a baby\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Three days later\add*, this woman¦157927 also gave¦157924 birth \add to her baby\add*. \add ≈Only the two¦157937 of us were there¦157931\add* in¦157935 the house—no \add ≈one else was around\add*.
\v 19 \add But\add* then¦157942 in the night¦157947, \add *her¦157948\add* son¦157943 died¦157942 because she¦157949 \add ≈rolled over onto\add* him¦157950.
\v 20 \add ≈So¦157952\add* she¦157952 \add ≈got up\add* in¦157963 the middle¦157953 of the night¦157954 and took my son from¦157959 beside¦157959 me, as your¦157960 female servant¦157960 was¦157961 asleep. She¦157962 \add ≈left her dead¦157967 son with¦157963 me, and took my son to her bed\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈When¦157971\add* I woke up in the morning¦157972 \add ready\add* to breastfeed my son, \add ≈to my horror\add* he¦157979 was dead. \add However\add* when I examined him¦157981 closely¦157980 in the light, more shock, it¦157986 wasn't \add actually\add* my son!”
\p
\v 22 “No¦157994, my son is the living¦157997 one,” the other¦157993 woman said¦158001, “and¦157998 your son is the dead¦157999 one.”
\p “No, \em your\em* son is the dead one,” the first¦158000 woman \add ≈countered\add*, “and \em my\em* son is the living one!”
\p Then¦157991 they¦158008 \add continued to\add* \add ≈argue¦158008 in¦158009 front¦158009 of¦158009\add* the¦157997 king¦158010.
\p
\v 23 The king¦158013 spoke, “\add ≈So¦158012 both of you are claiming that your baby is the one that's alive¦158019 and¦158012 that the dead one belongs to the other¦158022\add*.”
\v 24 Then \add *he¦158032\add* \add ≈ordered\add*, “Get me¦158035 a sword.” \add ≈So\add* they¦158038 brought¦158038 a sword to¦158040 the king¦158041.
\v 25 Then¦158043 the king¦158044 \add ≈commanded\add*, “\add ≈Cut¦158045\add* the living¦158049 child¦158048 into¦158050 two¦158050 pieces and¦158043 give¦158051 \add ≈them half each\add*.”
\p
\v 26 \add ≈But¦158061\add* the \add ≈mother of¦158065 the surviving baby\add* felt compassion¦158073 for¦158083 her son¦158076 and¦158061 \add ≈yelled\add*, “Please, my¦158080 master¦158080, give¦158081 the baby to¦158083 her—you certainly¦158088 mustn't \add ≈kill\add* him¦158091!”
\p \add ≈Meanwhile the¦158062 other¦158092 woman¦158062\add* was¦158093 saying¦158093, “\add ≈Well then¦158061, neither¦158094 of us will¦158101 have¦158072 him. Cut¦158102 him in half\add*!”
\p
\v 27 The king¦158105 \add ≈spoke up\add*, “Don't¦158115 harm the baby. Give¦158107 the living¦158113 child¦158112 to the \add first\add* woman—she's his¦158118 mother¦158118.”
\p
\v 28 All¦158121 Yisrael¦158123 \add eventually\add* heard¦158120 \add ≈about¦158121 this case\add* that the king had judged¦158126, and¦158120 they \add ≈felt an awesome respect for\add* \add *him\add* because¦158133 they saw¦158134 that he had God's¦158138 wisdom¦158137 to do¦158140 justice¦158141 within¦158139 him.
