\v 14 Then¦160894 while all the people stood¦160909 there, the king¦160895 turned¦160894 around¦160894 and¦160894 \add ≈pronounced a blessing¦160899\add* on all Yisrael¦160904,
\v 15 saying¦160911, “Blessed¦160912 is Yahweh¦160913, the god¦160914 of¦160914 Yisrael¦160915, who¦160916 spoke¦160917 \add ≈audibly to\add* my father¦160921 David¦160920, and¦160911 then¦160911 put into action the promise he'd given,
\v 16 ‘From the day¦160928 when¦160929 I brought¦160930 my people Yisrael out of Egypt¦160937, I didn't¦160938 choose a city¦160941 from \add among\add* all¦160942 the tribes¦160943 of Yisrael to build¦160945 a house¦160946 \add in\add* so that my name¦160948 would be \add established\add* there¦160949. \add ≈Instead\add* I chose¦160940 David¦160951 to \add ≈lead\add* my people Yisrael.’ ”\x + \xo 8:16: \xt 2Sam 7:4-11; 1Ch 17:3-10.\x*
