\v 22 Then Shelomoh¦161057 stood¦161056 \add ≈between\add* Yahweh's¦161060 altar¦161059 and all¦161062 the \add ≈gathered Israelis¦161065\add*, and \add ≈held his¦161067 arms up towards the sky\add*
\v 23 and \add ≈prayed\add*, “Yahweh¦161071, the god of¦161072 Yisrael¦161073, there's¦161074 no god¦161072 like¦161076 you in¦161078 the heavens¦161078 above¦161079 or \add here\add* on¦161078 the earth¦161082 below¦161083, keeping¦161084 the agreement¦161085 and \add showing\add* loyal¦161086 affection to¦161087 your¦161087 servants¦161087, the ones who¦161088 \add ≈serve you with¦161078 honest devotion\add*.
\v 24 \add ≈You¦161099 have done what you told your servant¦161096 David¦161097, my¦161098 father¦161098, that¦161100 you said you'd do\add*—you said it with your mouth¦161105 and¦161106 then put it into action with your hands as¦161108 \add we can see\add* today.
\v 25 Now¦161111, Yahweh¦161112, the god¦161114 of Yisrael, \add ≈do the other things\add* for your¦161117 servant¦161117 David¦161119 my¦161131 father¦161120, \add ≈when you told him¦161124 that¦161122 there'll always be¦161128 one of his descendants¦161141 on¦161133 Yisrael's¦161115 throne¦161135, provided they¦161140 follow you like he did\add*.\x + \xo 8:25: \xt 1Ki 2:4.\x*
\v 26 \add ≈So¦161151\add* now¦161151, God¦161152 of Yisrael¦161153, \add ≈show that¦161158 you're faithful to do what you say, by doing what you told\add* your¦161160 servant¦161160 David¦161161, my¦161162 father¦161162.
\p
\v 27 “\add ≈But¦161173\add* would God¦161167 really¦161165 reside on¦161168 the earth¦161170? The¦161171 sky and¦161173 the heavens¦161173 \add ≈aren't¦161175 big enough for you\add* so how could this¦161181 building¦161183 I've¦161183 constructed \add ≡contain¦161176 you\add*?\x + \xo 8:27: \xt 2Ch 2:6.\x*
\v 28 \add ≈But¦161185 still,\add* please give attention to your servant's prayer and¦161185 my request for favour, Yahweh¦161193 my god¦161194. \add Please\add* listen¦161195 to my \add ≈humble\add* prayer that¦161202 your servant is¦161204 praying¦161204 \add ≈to you¦161185 today\add*
\v 29 that your eyes¦161209 be on this house¦161213 night¦161215 and¦161216 day¦161216—the place that you've¦161221 said¦161221 \add ≈will be associated with your name¦161223\add*. \add ≈May you answer\add* the \add #prayers¦161228\add* that your servant¦161231 will pray¦161230 \add ≈towards\add* this place.\x + \xo 8:29: \xt Deu 12:11.\x*
\v 30 Listen¦161237 to¦161238 your servant's¦161241 plea for favour, and \add the prayers that\add* your people¦161242 Yisrael¦161243 will¦161245 pray¦161245 toward this place. \add ≈Keep listening¦161237 from where you live in\add* the heavens¦161258, and hear¦161259 and forgive¦161260.
\p
\v 31 “When someone¦161265 \add is accused of\add* sinning¦161264 against¦161266 his¦161266 neighbour¦161266 and says on¦161276 oath \add that the accusation is false\add*, and makes that oath in front¦161274 of your¦161275 altar¦161275 here in this¦161277 temple,
\v 32 then¦161279 you¦161281 should listen¦161281 from the heavens¦161282 and judge¦161284 your¦161287 people Yisrael¦161285, so that wicked people will¦161283 be condemned¦161288 \add ≈and bear the appropriate punishment\add*, and innocent people should be \add ≈declared¦161293 not guilty¦161289 and dealt with¦161292 appropriately\add*.
\p
\v 33 When¦161312 your people¦161301 Yisrael¦161302 are defeated¦161300 by an¦161304 enemy¦161304 because they've sinned¦161306 against you, and they turn¦161309 back to¦161310 you and confess¦161311 your name¦161314 and pray¦161315, and plead¦161316 for favour¦161316 toward you in¦161300 this¦161319 temple,
\v 34 then¦161321 you should listen¦161322 from the heavens¦161323 and forgive¦161324 the sin¦161325 of your people¦161326 Yisrael¦161327, and bring¦161328 them¦161328 back¦161328 to this land that¦161332 you gave¦161333 to our ancestors¦161334.
\p
\v 35 “\add Or when\add* the rain¦161342 \add ≈is held back in¦161337\add* the sky because¦161343 \add @your people\add* have sinned against you, and then they¦161344 pray¦161347 towards this¦161351 place¦161350 and \add ≈acknowledge you\add* and turn¦161357 away from¦161356 the \add ≈disobedience that¦161351 caused the problem\add*,
\v 36 then¦161361 \add ≈listen¦161363 to them from\add* the heavens¦161364 and forgive¦161365 the sin¦161366 of¦161366 your servants¦161367 and your people Yisrael¦161369, because¦161370 you'll direct \add ≈them towards the right way¦161374 to conduct themselves\add*. Then¦161361 you'll \add ≈send\add* rain¦161381 onto your land¦161384 that¦161376 you gave¦161387 to your people as an¦161389 inheritance¦161389.
\p
\v 37 “Suppose that there was a drought in the¦161396 land¦161412, or \add ≈diseases like\add* blight¦161401 or mildew¦161402, or \add ≈swarms of\add* locusts or grasshoppers, or if an enemy¦161411 \add ≈besieges them in a gated city\add*, or some other trouble or calamity,
\v 38 \add ≈then if anyone from¦161429\add* your¦161433 people¦161433 Yisrael¦161434 who¦161435 knows¦161436 \add ≈about¦161421 their own¦161439 disobedience\add* would spread¦161440 out¦161440 their palms¦161441 toward this¦161445 temple,
\v 39 then¦161447 \add ≈listen¦161448 to them from your¦161468 heavenly¦161449 abode\add* and forgive¦161452 their sin, and give¦161454 them \add ≈what they need\add*. You¦161453 and you alone¦161468 are the¦161471 only one who knows \add ≈what's inside a human¦161475 heart¦161471\add*.
\v 40 \add ≈Then\add* \add @the people\add* will¦161485 \add ≈want to obey\add* you \add ≈as long as they're alive¦161485\add* \add here\add* in the land that¦161482 you gave¦161491 to our¦161492 ancestors¦161492.
