\p
\v 1 \add ≈Once\add* Shelomoh¦162056 had¦162055 finished¦162055 the construction of the \add ≈temple and his palace, and various other projects of his\add*,
\v 2 Yahweh¦162078 appeared a second¦162082 time to \add *him\add*, \add ≈similar to his appearance\add* at¦162086 Gibeon¦162086\x + \xo 9:2: \xt 1Ki 3:5; 2Ch 1:7.\x*
\v 3 and said¦162088, “I've heard¦162091 your prayer¦162094 and your plea for favour¦162099 \add ≈requested from me\add*. I've \add ≈declared that\add* this¦162105 residence that you¦162107 built¦162107 \add ≈is holy\add* by¦162108 \add ≈associating my name¦162110 with it forever¦162114\add*, and my eyes and my heart will \add ≈constantly\add* be there.\f + \fr 9:3 \ft ‘my eyes and my heart’: many translations have something like ‘my presence’, but we've left it literal here for the reader to interpret rather than oversimplifying what we don't necessarily understand.\f*
\v 4 And as for you, if you'll¦162126 \add ≈behave with godliness\add* just¦162128 like your¦162131 father¦162131 David¦162130 \add ≈lived with total¦162137 dedication and honesty\add*, by \add ≈following everything\add* that¦162138 I've commanded¦162139 you including¦162135 keeping my statutes¦162140 and my judgements¦162141,
\v 5 then¦162144 I'll¦162158 \add ≈continue your dynasty over¦162149 Yisrael forever\add*, just¦162153 like I told your father¦162158 David¦162157 when I said¦162159, ‘\add ≈your descendants will¦162162 never be¦162162 removed\add* from¦162165 Yisrael's¦162151 throne.’\x + \xo 9:5: \xt 1Ki 2:4.\x*
\v 6 If¦162181 you or your descendants¦162174 ever¦162171 turn back from¦162175 \add ≈following¦162175\add* me¦162175 and don't¦162176 keep¦162177 my commands¦162178 and statutes¦162179, and you go¦162183 and serve¦162184 other¦162186 gods¦162185 and bow¦162187 down¦162187 to¦162188 them¦162188,
\v 7 then¦162190 I'll cut¦162190 Yisrael off¦162190 from \add ≈the land\add* that I've¦162198 given¦162198 them and from the \add ≈temple that's dedicated to¦162199\add* my¦162205 name¦162205—I'll send¦162206 \add >them\add* \add ≈far\add* away¦162206, and Yisrael will¦162206 \add ≈become an example and a laughing stock\add* among all¦162213 the \add other\add* \add ≈countries\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈As this temple is on a hill and very visible\add*, everyone¦162221 who passes¦162223 \add anywhere\add* nearby \add will see it and\add* will be¦162225 appalled¦162225 and will hiss¦162226 and they'll say¦162227, ‘\add What did the people do\add* \add ≈that was so¦162233 bad that\add* Yahweh¦162232 did that to this country and to this temple?’\x + \xo 9:8: \xt 2Ki 25:9; 2Ch 36:19.\x*
\v 9 Then¦162239 they'll \add ≈answer\add*, ‘\add It's\add* because they abandoned¦162242 their god¦162246 Yahweh who¦162247 brought their ancestors¦162251 out of Egypt¦162253, \add ≈but¦162239\add* they held¦162254 on¦162255 to other¦162256 gods¦162255 and bowed¦162257 down¦162257 to them and served¦162261 them. Therefore¦162262 Yahweh brought all¦162269 this¦162272 \add ≈calamity¦162271\add* onto them.’ ”
\s1 King Hiram gains some poor cities
\rem /s1 Solomon's Agreement with Hiram; Solomon's Other Activities
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (2 Chr. 8:1-2)
\p
\v 10 \add ≈It¦162275 took\add* twenty¦162277 years¦162278 for Shelomoh¦162282 to construct \add ≈the temple for Yahweh¦162290 and¦162291 the palace for himself\add*.
\v 11 King Hiram¦162316 from Tsor¦162299 \add !(Tyre¦162299)\add*, had¦162300 supported¦162300 Shelomoh with cedar¦162305 and cypress¦162307 \add ≈logs\add*, and with gold¦162308—\add ≈as much as he'd needed. So\add* King Shelomoh gave¦162313 \add *him\add* twenty¦162317 cities in¦162304 the¦162320 Galilee¦162320 \add ≈region¦162319\add*,
\v 12 \add ≈but¦162322 when\add* Hiram¦162323 came \add ≈down\add* from¦162324 Tsor¦162324 to¦162325 see¦162325 the¦162328 cities¦162328 that¦162329 Shelomoh¦162333 had¦162330 given¦162330 him, \add ≈he wasn't very happy about¦162336 them\add*
\v 13 and \add ≈asked\add*, “My friend, what¦162339 \add sort of\add* cities¦162340 are¦162340 these¦162341 that¦162342 you've¦162344 given¦162344 me¦162345?” and he¦162347 called the area ‘Kabul’ \add (meaning ‘Worthless’), which it's still called\add* to¦162348 this¦162353 day¦162352.
\v 14 Hiram¦162357 \add had\add* sent¦162356 four tonnes of gold¦162362 to Shelomoh.
\s1 Shelomoh's other achievements
\rem /s1 Further Achievements of Solomon; Other Acts of Solomon; Solomon's Many Achievements
