\v 26 Nebat's¦163672 son¦163670 Yarave'am¦163669 \add !(Jeroboam¦163669)\add*, an¦163673 Efratite¦163673 from¦163674 Tseredah¦163676 \add also\add* \add ≈rebelled against the¦163676 king¦163686\add*. (His¦163678 widowed¦163681 mother¦163678 Tseruah¦163679 was¦163679 one of¦163683 Shelomoh's¦163683 servants¦163682.)
\v 27 \add ≈This¦163699 is¦163689 the background about¦163703 how it started\add*: Shelomoh¦163695 had built¦163696 the raised¦163692 terrace and¦163688 had \add ≈repaired a gap in¦163694 the wall\add* of the city¦163704 of David¦163705 his¦163706 father¦163706.
