\v 31 and told Yarave'am, “Take¦163764 ten pieces¦163768 for yourself¦163783, because¦163769 this is what Yisrael's¦163774 god¦163773 Yahweh¦163772 says¦163771, ‘Listen, I'm¦163775 about¦163776 to tear¦163776 the kingdom¦163779 away from¦163780 Shelomoh's¦163781 \add ≈control\add*, and I'll¦163782 give¦163782 the\f + \fr 11:31 \ft Most English translations leave out this ‘the’ (which is in the Hebrew). However, we suspect that both Ahiyah and Yarave'am knew exactly which of the ten tribes it would be.\f* ten tribes to you.
\v 32 The one tribe\f + \fr 11:32 \ft It would have been obvious at the time that this was referring to Yehudah. (The unmentioned twelfth tribe is Benyamin—the youngest brother and the smallest tribe.)\f* will¦163790 be for him¦163792, for the sake of my¦163795 servant¦163795 David¦163796 and for the sake of Yerushalem¦163798 city¦163799 which¦163800 I've¦163801 chosen¦163801 from¦163803 all¦163803 the tribes¦163804 of Yisrael¦163805.
