\p
\v 1 Then a \add ≈prophet from\add* of God¦164766 came¦164767 from Yehudah¦164768, \add taking\add* Yahweh's¦164770 message¦164769 to Beyt¦164773-El. as Yarave'am¦164776 \add !(Jeroboam¦164776)\add* was¦164777 standing¦164777 by the¦164780 altar¦164780 to burn incense¦164781.
\v 2 \add @The¦164786 prophet\add* called¦164783 out against the altar¦164786 with¦164787 Yahweh's¦164788 message¦164787: “Altar! Altar! Yahweh says¦164793 this: Listen, \add one of\add* \add ≈David's¦164801 descendants\add* will have a son¦164797 \add ≈who'll be named\add* Yoshiyah¦164802 \add !(Josiah¦164802)\add*, and¦164783 he'll¦164804 sacrifice¦164804 the priests¦164808 \add ≈from the hill temples\add* on you—the ones who are burning incense¦164810 on you. \add Yes,\add* human¦164813 bones¦164812 will be burnt on you.”\x + \xo 13:2: \xt 2Ki 23:15-16.\x*
\v 3 Then¦164817 he \add ≈offered them evidence that what he said¦164821 came from\add* Yahweh¦164826, “Listen¦164827, that altar¦164828 will be¦164829 \add ≈broken\add* into pieces, and¦164817 the ashes¦164831 in it¦164830 will \add ≈spill all over the ground\add*.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈The moment\add* the King¦164838 Yarave'am¦164854 heard¦164837 the message¦164841 that the man of¦164842 God¦164844 had¦164866 called out¦164846 against the altar at Beyt-El, \add ≈he called for the man to be arrested\add*. \add ≈However,\add* the arm that he used to point to him¦164862 over the altar \add ≈suddenly became paralysed\add* and¦164836 he wasn't able¦164869 to \add ≈pull it¦164870 back¦164870\add*.
