\v 11 Now \add at that time there was\add* an old¦165012 prophet¦165010 who lived in Beyt-El, and his sons\f + \fr 13:11 \ft This is singular in the Hebrew, but the rest of this segment suggests multiple sons.\f* had been and told him all the news about¦165014 what that man¦165030 of God¦165032 had done¦165029 that day¦165034 in Beyt-El and they¦165046 told him the message¦165040 that \add ≈had been passed on\add* to¦165043 the king¦165045.
