\v 15 “\add ≈Come¦165109 home¦165111 with¦165110 me¦165110 and¦165112 have something to¦165111 eat¦165112\add*.” he¦165107 \add ≈invited\add* him¦165108.
\p
\v 16 “\add Sorry,\add*” he¦165115 \add ≈replied\add*. “I \add ≈can't go¦165120 with you or visit your home\add*, and¦165115 I \add ≈can't eat¦165124 or drink¦165128\add* with you in¦165131 this¦165132 place¦165131,
\v 17 because¦165134 Yahweh¦165139 \add ≈instructed\add* me¦165137 \add ≈not to eat¦165142 or drink¦165146 here, or to go¦165152 home by the same road that¦165154 I came on¦165138\add*.”
\p
\v 18 Then¦165159 \add @the old prophet\add* told him¦165172, “I'm¦165163 also¦165161 a prophet like¦165165 you, and Yahweh¦165170 sent a messenger¦165169 to tell me \add ≈that I should take you home with¦165169 me so you can have¦165167 something to eat¦165177 and drink¦165179\add*.” (\add ≈But¦165159 that was a lie\add*.)
\p
\v 19 \add ≈So¦165184\add* \add @the prophet\add* \add ≈accompanied him¦165185 to his¦165188 house¦165188 and¦165184 had a meal there\add*.
\v 20 Then¦165192 while they¦165193 were¦165194 \add ≈still\add* seated at the table¦165197, Yahweh¦165202 spoke through the \add ≈old prophet¦165205\add*,
\v 21 and he¦165209 called¦165209 out to¦165210 the¦165212 man¦165212 of¦165212 God¦165235 who'd come¦165216 from¦165217 Yehudah¦165217, “Yahweh says¦165220 this: Because you have¦165224 been rebellious¦165224 against¦165224 Yahweh and \add ≈because¦165222 you didn't¦165227 obey what Yahweh instructed¦165233\add* you
\v 22 and you've returned¦165237 and you've \add ≈had food¦165239 and drink\add* in the place¦165242 where he¦165244 told you \add ≈not to eat¦165248 or drink\add*, your \add ≈body¦165257 won't¦165246 be buried in your home town\add*.”
\p
\v 23 After \add ≈the meal was finished\add*, \add @the old prophet\add* saddled¦165269 the donkey¦165272 for¦165273 the prophet that he'd brought¦165275 back,
\v 24 and he left. \add ≈But¦165277\add* on the road, a lion \add ≈came across him\add* and killed¦165281 him. His¦165283 corpse¦165283 \add ≈ended up\add* lying on the road with¦165280 the donkey¦165286 standing beside it, and the lion also standing beside \add *it\add*.
\v 25 \add ≈Some passers-by\add* saw¦165297 the corpse¦165300 on¦165302 the road¦165302 and \add the unusual sight of\add* the lion¦165305 standing¦165306 beside¦165307 \add *it¦165316\add*, and \add ≈when they got to\add* the city¦165311 where the old¦165314 prophet¦165313 lived, they \add ≈told everyone the news\add*.
\p
\v 26 \add ≈When¦165318\add* the prophet¦165319 who had brought¦165321 him back from¦165322 the road heard he¦165325 said, “\add ≈That will be\add* the man¦165326 of God¦165327 who was rebellious¦165330 against¦165330 Yahweh. Yahweh \add ≈must have given¦165335\add* him to the lion¦165337, and it¦165338 tore him into pieces and put him to death according¦165340 what Yahweh \add ≈had said would happen\add*.”
\v 27 Then¦165347 he¦165347 told his¦165350 sons¦165350, “Saddle¦165352 the donkey¦165357 for me.” They \add ≈put the saddle¦165352 on\add*,
\v 28 and he went¦165360 and found¦165361 the body lying on¦165366 the road¦165366, and the donkey and the lion standing¦165369 by \add *it\add*. The¦165375 lion hadn't eaten¦165374 any of the man of God's body, nor had it attacked the donkey.
\v 29 The¦165387 prophet¦165386 lifted the body and \add ≈laid it across\add* the donkey¦165396 and brought¦165397 it back to his city¦165401 to be buried¦165405 in his own tomb.
\v 30 They wailed over him¦165413, saying, “Oh dear, my¦165415 brother¦165415,” and¦165412 they laid his body¦165410 in¦165411 \add @the old prophet's\add* grave¦165411.
\v 31 \add ≈When the period of mourning was¦165417 over,\add* he told his sons¦165424, “When I¦165426 die¦165426, bury¦165427 me¦165428 in¦165426 the grave¦165429 where the man¦165431 of God¦165432 is¦165433 buried¦165433. \add ≈My bones will end up\add* beside¦165435 his bones.
\v 32 The¦165445 message¦165445 from Yahweh¦165449 that¦165446 he¦165447 shouted out¦165447 against the altar¦165452 in Beyt-El will¦165463 certainly¦165443 happen, and¦165457 against all¦165458 the \add ≈hilltop¦165461 worship\add* places¦165461 in Shomron¦165464 \add !(Samaria¦165464)\add*.
\s1 Yarave'am's fatal sin
