\p
\v 1 At¦165504 that¦165505 time¦165504, \add one of\add* Yarave'am's¦165510 sons, Aviyyah¦165507, became¦165506 very sick¦165506
\v 2 and Yarave'am¦165513 told his wife, “\add ≈Go and get changed so that no one will¦165524 recognise you¦165522 as\add* \add *my\add* wife. Then¦165512 go¦165526 to¦165537 Shiloh¦165527 where the prophet¦165532 Ahiyah¦165531 is—he's \add ≈the one who prophesied that I'd become¦165537 king¦165537\add*.
\v 3 Take¦165543 ten¦165545 loaves of bread¦165546 and \add some\add* cakes¦165547 and a jar¦165548 of honey¦165549 to give to him. He'll tell¦165553 you¦165544 what¦165555 will¦165557 happen¦165557 to the boy¦165558.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦165560\add* \add *his\add* wife¦165562 \add ≈got ready\add* and went¦165565 to Ahiyah's¦165569 house¦165568 at Shiloh¦165566. Ahiyah was \add ≈now very elderly and\add* not¦165571 able¦165573 to see¦165574,
\v 5 \add ≈but¦165581\add* Yahweh¦165581 had¦165582 told \add *him\add*, “Listen, Yarave'am's¦165588 wife¦165587 will be coming to \add ≈ask for your guidance\add* about¦165589 her son¦165595, because¦165596 he's¦165599 sick¦165598. \add ≈I want you¦165602 to tell her so-and-so. And¦165604 when she comes¦165605, she won't be dressed like a queen\add*.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦165609\add* as soon as Ahiyah¦165611 heard¦165610 her¦165615 \add ≈walk through the¦165614 doorway\add*, he¦165618 said¦165618, “Come¦165619 in¦165617, wife¦165620 of¦165620 Yarave'am¦165621. Why \add ≈did you get changed like that¦165623\add*? Now I've¦165626 been¦165627 \add ≈instructed to¦165628 pass bad news¦165629 onto\add* you—
\v 7 go \add back\add* and \add ≈give Yarave'am¦165633 this message from\add* Yisrael's¦165639 god¦165638 Yahweh¦165637, ‘I¦165642 \add ≈chose you out from\add* the¦165644 people and \add ≈placed\add* you as a leader¦165646 over¦165647 my people Yisrael,
\v 8 and I tore¦165651 the kingdom¦165654 away from¦165655 \add ≈David's¦165656 descendants\add* and gave¦165657 it¦165657 to¦165658 you. \add ≈But¦165651\add* you haven't been¦165661 like¦165662 my servant¦165662 David who¦165664 \add ≈obeyed my instructions and followed me with¦165677 integrity—only¦165675 doing¦165674 what he knew that¦165667 I approved of\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈However,\add* you've¦165695 done¦165679 more evil¦165679 \add things\add* than any of those¦165682 who \add ≈ruled before you\add*. You've \add ≈rejected me\add* and made¦165687 cast images¦165692 of other¦165691 gods¦165690, and have provoked¦165693 me into anger¦165693.
\v 10 \add ≈Because of that\add*, I'm¦165701 about¦165702 to bring¦165702 calamity¦165703 to \add *your\add* \add ≈family\add*: I'll \add ≈cause all your male descendants to die, either before or after they've left home\add*. I'll \add ≈eliminate your family\add* just¦165720 like \add dried\add* dung¦165722 burns until¦165723 it's¦165725 \add ≈all gone\add*.\x + \xo 14:10: \xt 1Ki 15:29.\x*
\v 11 The \add family members\add* who die in the city¦165729 will be eaten by dogs¦165731, and¦165732 those who die in the countryside¦165733 will be eaten by birds. \add All this\add* \add ≈comes from\add* Yahweh¦165738.’
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So¦165741 go¦165743 back home\add*, \add but\add* \add ≈as soon as you¦165741 set foot in¦165745\add* the city¦165747, your son will¦165748 die¦165748.
\v 13 All¦165754 Yisrael will¦165757 \add ≈mourn¦165751\add* for him and¦165757 they'll¦165751 bury¦165757 him. \add ≈He'll be the only one of your children to be buried\add*, because¦165768 \add ≈out of all of Yarave'am's¦165764 descendants, he's the only one that¦165761\add* Yisrael's¦165756 god¦165777 Yahweh¦165776 found¦165769 good¦165773 in.
\v 14 \add ≈In the future,\add* Yahweh¦165783 will \add ≈appoint\add* for himself, a king¦165785 over¦165786 Yisrael¦165788 who¦165789 will \add ≈get rid of¦165793 Yarave'am's¦165794 descendants\add*—\add in fact\add* \add ≈it's beginning to come about¦165793\add* even now¦165800.
