\v 22 \add The people of\add* Yehudah¦165955 did¦165963 what Yahweh¦165958 \add ≈had decided was\add* evil¦165956—\add in fact\add* they¦165959 made¦165959 him¦165960 more jealous¦165959 \add (by worshipping other gods)\add* than their¦165965 ancestors¦165964 \add ≈ever had\add*.
\v 23 They¦165976 even built¦165969 \add ≈hilltop¦165974 temples\add* and sacred¦165975 pillars¦165975 and poles¦165976 on¦165977 every high¦165974 hill¦165980 and under¦165982 every \add ≈large evergreen\add* tree¦165985.\x + \xo 14:23: \xt 2Ki 17:9-10.\x*
\v 24 There were also¦165988 male¦165990 prostitutes¦165990 \add ≈associated with them\add*, and¦165988 \add @the Israelis¦166002\add* did¦165993 the same abhorrent things as the nations¦165996 that¦165997 Yahweh¦165999 had¦165998 removed ahead of¦166000 \add their entering the land\add*.\x + \xo 14:24: \xt Deu 23:17.\x*
