\v 25 In¦166006 the fifth¦166007 year¦166006 of King Rehavam's \add reign\add*, Egypt's¦166015 King Shishak¦166011 \add ≈attacked\add* Yerushalem¦166018\x + \xo 14:25: \xt 2Ch 12:2-8.\x*
\v 26 and took away the valuables from Yahweh's¦166026 temple, and the king's¦166031 palace. He took everything¦166034 \add of value\add*, including¦166027 all the gold¦166042 shields¦166041 that¦166043 Shelomoh¦166045 had¦166044 made¦166044.\x + \xo 14:26: \xt 1Ki 10:16-17; 2Ch 9:15-16.\x*
\v 27 \add ≈To replace¦166050 them,\add* King¦166048 Rehavam made¦166047 \add some\add* bronze¦166052 shields¦166051 and¦166047 \add ≈assigned them to the officers who¦166059 protect the entrance¦166060 to the palace\add*.
\v 28 \add ≈Whenever¦166070\add* the king¦166068 would enter the \add ≈temple, the guards¦166072 would quickly take the shields there, and¦166064 when he left, they'd run them¦166073 back to¦166074 the palace\add*.
