\v 11 Asa¦166294 did \add ≈what was pleasing to\add* Yahweh¦166297, like¦166298 his¦166299 ancestor David¦166298 \add had done\add*,
\v 12 and he¦166301 \add ≈expelled the male¦166302 prostitutes¦166302 from¦166303 the country\add* and removed¦166306 all¦166309 the idols¦166311 \add ≈made¦166313 by the previous generations\add*.\x + \xo 15:12: \xt 2Ch 15:8-15.\x*
\v 13 He also¦166316 removed¦166322 his¦166321 grandmother Maakah¦166320 from¦166323 being queen-mother¦166323 because she¦166326 had¦166326 made¦166326 a horrid Asherah \add ≈goddess\add*, then¦166316 \add *he¦166329\add* cut¦166329 down¦166329 her¦166333 horrid \add ≈idol\add* and¦166316 burnt¦166334 it in¦166335 the¦166335 Kidron¦166336 \add ≈valley\add*.
\v 14 He¦166345 didn't¦166339 remove¦166341 the \add ≈hilltop¦166338 temples\add*, \add but despite that\add* \add ≈he was¦166346 fully devoted to\add* Yahweh¦166350 all¦166351 \add ≈his¦166353 life\add*.
\v 15 He¦166355 brought¦166355 \add ≈everything that father¦166359 had dedicated, plus¦166360 more of¦166358 his¦166359 own, into Yahweh's¦166363 temple\add*, \add including\add* gold¦166365, silver¦166364, and¦166355 containers.
