\p
\v 16 Asa¦166371 and¦166372 King¦166374 Baasha¦166373 of Yisrael¦166376 \add ≈were in a continual state of war¦166368 during their¦166379 reigns\add*.
\v 17 King Baasha¦166382 invaded Yehudah and¦166381 \add ≈fortified\add* Ramah¦166392 \add ≈so that no one¦166395 could pass in or out¦166395 to¦166397 help\add* King Asa¦166397 of¦166398 Yehudah.
\v 18 \add ≈So¦166401\add* Asa¦166402 took¦166401 all¦166405 the remaining¦166409 gold¦166408 and silver¦166407 from the \add ≈temple and palace\add* storerooms, and \add ≈sent¦166425 it with¦166411\add* his servants¦166424 \add ≈to take\add* to Ben¦166430-Hadad¦166432, son of Tabrimmon¦166435, son of King¦166426 Hezion¦166438 of Aram¦166440 who¦166441 lived¦166441 in¦166411 Damascus¦166442, \add ≈to tell him\add*,
\v 19 “\add ≈You and me have an agreement between¦166448 us that was made by our two fathers¦166449\add*, so look, I've sent¦166453 a present of gold¦166457 and silver¦166456 to you¦166447. \add ≈So then,\add* break¦166459 your¦166462 agreement with¦166463 King¦166466 Baasha¦166465 of Yisrael¦166468 \add ≈so he'll give up¦166469 on¦166470 attacking\add* me.”
\p
\v 20 Ben¦166473-Hadad¦166475 \add ≈did what king¦166478 Asa¦166479 requested\add*, and he¦166480 sent¦166480 the¦166483 commanders¦166483 of¦166483 \add ≈his best warriors\add* to¦166487 attack¦166492 Israeli¦166490 cities¦166490 \add ≈including¦166480\add* Iyon¦166495, Dan¦166498, Avel¦166500-Beyt¦166501-Maakah¦166503, and all Kinnerot along with¦166508 all Naftali¦166512 \add ≈region¦166511\add*.
\v 21 When¦166514 \add King\add* Baasha¦166516 heard¦166515 \add >about that\add*, he stopped¦166517 \add ≈fortifying\add* Ramah¦166521 and¦166514 \add ≈withdrew\add* to Tirtsah¦166523.
