\p
\v 33 Ahiyah's¦166767 son¦166765 Baasha¦166764 \add began\add* to reign over Yisrael¦166772 in¦166773 the third year¦166758 of King¦166761 Asa's¦166760 \add reign\add* over Yehudah¦166762, and¦166775 he ruled from Tirtsah¦166773 for twenty-four¦166774 years¦166776.
\v 34 He did \add ≈what Yahweh¦166781 had said was\add* evil¦166779, \add ≈similar to Nabat's son Yarave'am's¦166784 behaviour\add* and¦166778 his sin that¦166786 \add in turn\add*, caused¦166787 Yisrael¦166790 to sin.
\c 16
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦166796 \add ≈told Hanani's¦166802 son¦166800 Yehu¦166799 to tell\add* Baasha¦166805,
\v 2 “I¦166810 \add ≈took a nobody and promoted you to\add* leader¦166815 over¦166816 my people Yisrael, \add ≈yet\add* you \add ≈followed Yarave'am's¦166822 behaviour\add* and provoked¦166828 me to anger¦166828 by causing¦166823 my people Yisrael to sin¦166823,
\v 3 \add ≈so now I'll get rid of you and your¦166840 family—I'll do the same to you that I did to Yarave'am¦166842 and his family\add*.
\v 4 \add The bodies of\add* \add ≈those in your family who die in the city¦166849 will be eaten by dogs¦166851, and¦166852 those who die in the countryside¦166854 will be eaten by vultures\add*.
\p
\v 5 \add ≈Everything else that¦166862 Baasha¦166861 did¦166863 is written¦166868 in the book of the events\add* of the kings¦166874 of Yisrael¦166875.
\v 6 \add ≈When¦166877 Baasha¦166878 died\add* he was¦166882 buried¦166882 in¦166883 Tirtsah¦166883, and¦166877 his¦166887 son¦166886 Elah¦166885 \add ≈replaced him¦166887 as king¦166884\add*.
\p
\v 7 Yahweh \add ≈sent that message¦166897 via Hanani¦166895 the prophet's¦166896 son¦166893 Yehu¦166892. It¦166900 was for Baasha and¦166889 his¦166906 family—speaking against¦166901 the evil¦166910 that they'd done¦166914 that had provoked¦166918 Yahweh to¦166904 get angry with their behaviour which¦166912 was as bad as Yarave'am's family had been. Yahweh was also angry with Baasha because he¦166914 had killed all of Yarave'am's family\add*.
