\v 8 Baasha's¦166942 son Elah¦166939 \add began\add* to reign in¦166946 the twenty-sixth¦166932 year of King¦166936 Asa's¦166935 \add reign\add* over Yehudah¦166937, and¦166933 he ruled from Tirtsah¦166946 for two¦166947 years¦166947.
\v 9 \add ≈However,\add* his¦166951 servant¦166951 Zimri¦166952 who was the commander¦166953 of half¦166954 of the chariots¦166955 conspired¦166949 against him. \add ≈Once when\add* \add @Elah\add* was in Tirtsah¦166957 \add ≈getting\add* himself drunk¦166959 at¦166957 the house¦166960 of Arza¦166961 (who was \add ≈in charge of the palace¦166965\add*),
\v 10 Zimri¦166969 went¦166968 in and \add ≈attacked and killed¦166971\add* him¦166971, and \add ≈took over his¦166979 place¦166979 as king\add*. (That was in the twenty-seventh¦166973 year¦166972 of¦166979 King¦166976 Asa's¦166975 \add reign\add* over Yehudah¦166977.)
\p
\v 11 \add ≈As soon as Zimri took over and¦166981\add* sat¦166983 on¦166982 his¦166986 throne¦166986, he \add ≈had all¦166990 of¦166992 Baasha's¦166993 family executed—he didn't¦166994 leave¦166996 a single male\add* or relative or friend¦167001.
\v 12 \add In that way,\add* Zimri¦167004 \add ≈eliminated all¦167006 of¦167008 Baasha's¦167009 descendants just as Yahweh¦167011 had¦167013 said via\add* the prophet¦167019 Yehu¦167018
\v 13 concerning all¦167022 of Baasha's¦167025 sins and the¦167026 sins of his¦167028 son¦167028 Elah¦167027, and because they¦167032 caused¦167032 Yisrael to sin¦167032 by provoking¦167036 Yisrael's¦167035 god¦167040 Yahweh¦167039 to get angry with¦167042 their¦167042 idols¦167042.
\v 14 \add ≈Everything else that¦167049 Elah¦167046 did¦167050 is written¦167054 in the book of the events\add* of the kings¦167060 of Yisrael¦167061.
