\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 15 Zimri¦167072 reigned from Tirtsah¦167075 for seven¦167066 days¦167074 in¦167075 the twenty-seventh¦167065 year¦167067 of King¦167069 Asa's¦167068 \add reign\add* over Yehudah¦167070. \add At the time,\add* \add ≈the Israeli army were¦167077 besieging the Philistine city of\add* Gibbeton¦167080,
\v 16 and \add ≈when the army\add* camped \add around the city\add* heard \add ≈that Zimri¦167089 had rebelled and assassinated\add* the king, that day¦167108 all¦167096 the people¦167085 in¦167110 the camp¦167110 \add ≈installed\add* the army commander¦167102 Omri¦167107 \add as king\add* to reign over¦167105 Yisrael¦167098.
\v 17 \add ≈So¦167112\add* Omri¦167113 \add ≈took all¦167114 his warriors\add* from¦167118 Gibbeton¦167118 and¦167112 besieged¦167119 Tirtsah¦167122.
\v 18 \add ≈As¦167140 soon as¦167125\add* Zimri¦167126 \add ≈realised¦167125 that¦167127 the city¦167130 was surrounded\add*, he¦167131 went¦167131 into¦167132 the \add ≈saferoom in the palace\add* and \add ≈set fire¦167145 to the building and died¦167146 in the flames¦167145\add*
\v 19 because \add ≈he'd done what Yahweh¦167157 had said was evil¦167155—following Yarave'am's¦167160 behaviour including¦167161\add* causing¦167164 Yisrael¦167167 to¦167158 sin.
\v 20 \add ≈Everything else that¦167173 Zimri¦167171 did, including¦167172 his¦167172 rebellion, is written¦167178 in the book of the events\add* of the kings¦167184 of Yisrael¦167185.
