\p
\v 29 Omri's¦167345 son¦167343 Ahav¦167358 \add ≈became¦167346 king¦167346 of Israel¦167349\add* in¦167365 the¦167355 thirty-eighth¦167351 year¦167368 of King¦167346 Ahab's¦167342 \add reign\add* over¦167362 Yehudah¦167356, and¦167367 he¦167357 reigned¦167357 Yisrael¦167349 from Shomron¦167365 for twenty-two¦167366 years¦167368.
\v 30 Ahav¦167371 did \add ≈what Yahweh¦167377 had said was\add* evil—\add in fact\add* he did more evil things than all¦167378 those¦167379 \add kings\add* who¦167379 \add ≈preceded\add* him¦167380.
\rem /s1 Ahab Marries Jezebel and Worships Baal
\v 31 \add ≈As if following Yarave'am's¦167386 behaviour wasn't bad enough, he married\add* Izevel¦167394 \add !(Jezebel¦167394)\add*, the daughter¦167395 of the Sidonian King¦167398 Etbaal¦167397, then¦167382 went¦167400 and served¦167401 Baal¦167404 and bowed¦167405 down¦167405 to¦167406 him¦167406.
\v 32 He¦167412 \add ≈built¦167414 a temple for Baal¦167410 in Shomron¦167415 and¦167408 placed an¦167409 altar¦167409 in it\add*.
\v 33 Ahav¦167418 \add also\add* made¦167417 an Asherah¦167421 pole¦167421 and¦167422 went on to provoke¦167425 Yisrael's¦167430 god¦167429 Yahweh¦167428 to get angry, more than any of the¦167432 \add ≈previous\add* kings¦167432 of Yisrael \add had done\add*.
\v 34 \add ≈During his reign\add*, Hiel¦167440 from Beyt¦167441-El \add ≈rebuilt¦167439 Yeriho¦167445\add* \add !(Jericho¦167445)\add* \add ≈city. As they laid the foundations¦167448, his eldest son Aviram¦167446 died, and¦167449 when they hung the city gates¦167453\add*, his youngest¦167451 son Seguv¦167449 died, just as Yahweh¦167455 had told (Nun's¦167462 son) Yehoshua¦167459 \add !(Joshua)\add*.\x + \xo 16:34: \xt Josh 6:26.\x*
\c 17
\s1 Eliyah prophesies about a coming drought
\rem /s1 Elijah Fed by Ravens; Elijah and the Drought; Elijah Predicts a Drought
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add One day the prophet\add* Eliyah¦167466 \add !(Elijah¦167466)\add* from the Tishbites¦167467 in the Gilead¦167469 region said¦167465 to Ahav¦167472, “As Yisrael's¦167477 god¦167476 Yahweh¦167475 \add ≈lives, the one who I serve\add*, there won't be any rain or \add even\add* dew these¦167485 \add next\add* years¦167484 unless \add ≈I give the command\add*.”\x + \xo 17:1: \xt Jam 5:17.\x*
\v 2 Then Yahweh¦167498 \add ≈told\add* \add @Eliyah\add*,
\v 3 “\add ≈Get away from¦167503 here¦167503 and travel\add* eastward¦167506 \add ≈towards the Kerit¦167509 stream that¦167510 enters\add* the Yordan¦167514 \add river\add* \add ≈to hide¦167507\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈You'll be able\add* to drink¦167518 from¦167517 the stream, and¦167516 I've¦167522 commanded¦167522 the ravens¦167521 to \add ≈bring food to\add* you¦167523 there¦167524.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦167526 he did what Yahweh¦167529 told him, and went¦167530 and lived¦167531 by the Kerit¦167533 stream near\add* the Yordan¦167538.
\v 6 Ravens¦167540 brought¦167541 bread and meat to him \add every\add* morning¦167545 and \add ≈again\add* in¦167545 the evening¦167548, and he was able to drink¦167552 from¦167549 the stream.
\rem /s1 The Widow at Zarephath
\v 7 \add ≈However, the stream dried¦167557 up¦167557 after a while because¦167559 there was no rain¦167563 anywhere in the country\add*.
\s1 Eliyah and the widow at Tserefat
\rem /s1 The Widow at Zarephath; Elijah and the Widow in Zarephath; The Widow of Zarephath
\p
\v 8 Then Yahweh¦167570 \add ≈told\add* \add @Eliyah\add*,
\v 9 “\add ≈Leave here\add* \add and\add* go¦167575 to Tserefat¦167576 in the Tsidon¦167578 \add region\add* and stay¦167579 there. Listen, I've¦167582 commanded¦167582 a widow¦167585 lady there \add ≈to keep you¦167586 fed\add*.”\x + \xo 17:9: \xt Luk 4:25-26.\x*
\v 10 \add ≈So¦167588 he got ready\add* and went¦167590 to¦167591 Tserefat¦167591. \add ≈As he entered the town¦167596, he saw a woman¦167600 picking up bits of firewood, and he asked her¦167605, “Can you please¦167609 get¦167607 me¦167610 a drink¦167615 of water¦167613\add*.”
\v 11 As she¦167617 went¦167617 to get¦167622 it, he called¦167619 out, “\add ≈Would you have a piece¦167626 of bread¦167628 to go with¦167629 it?\add*.”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈But¦167631 she¦167631 replied\add*, “As your¦167635 god¦167635 Yahweh¦167634 \add ≈lives, I don't have any bread at¦167649 all\add*—only a \add ≈handful\add* of flour¦167648 in the jar¦167649, and a little bit of oil¦167652 in the jug¦167653. See, I'm¦167654 gathering¦167655 \add ≈a few bits of firewood so I can make a little bread\add* for me¦167660 and my¦167661 son¦167661. \add ≈After we've eaten¦167662 that\add*, then¦167631 we'll¦167662 die¦167663.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈But¦167665\add* Eliyah¦167667 told her¦167666, “Don't¦167668 be \add ≈worried. Go¦167671 and do¦167672 what you said¦167665\add*, except make some bread¦167679 for me first¦167681 and bring¦167682 it out¦167682 to¦167684 me. Then¦167665 \add ≈after¦167688 that, you can make some\add* for you and for your¦167673 son¦167686,
\v 14 because¦167691 Yisrael's¦167696 god¦167695 Yahweh \add ≈has told me that your flour¦167698 won't run out and¦167701 your oil¦167702 won't come to an¦167700 end¦167700\add* until¦167705 the day¦167706 when Yahweh gives¦167707 \add ≈us rain¦167711 again\add*.”
\p
\v 15 \add ≈So¦167717 the woman went¦167717 and did¦167718 what Eliyah said\add*, then¦167717 \add sure enough\add* \add @Eliyah\add* and \add @the widow\add* and her¦167726 household¦167726 \add ≈had enough food every day\add*.
\v 16 The jar¦167729 of flour¦167730 \add ≈never got empty\add* and the jug¦167733 of oil¦167734 \add ≈never ran out, just as Yahweh¦167738 had promised via\add* Eliyah¦167742.
\rem /s1 Elijah Revives the Widow's Son
\p
\v 17 \add ≈Some time afterwards¦167746,\add* the woman's¦167752 son¦167750 got sick¦167749 and¦167755 then \add ≈it¦167755 got so bad that¦167760 he died\add*,
\v 18 \add ≈so\add* she¦167768 hassled Eliyah¦167771, “You¦167775 man¦167776 of¦167776 God, \add ≈why did you¦167778 come¦167778 here! Now my sins have¦167778 been brought¦167780 to God's mind, and¦167768 he's caused¦167784 my son¦167787 to die!\add*”
\p
\v 19 \add ≈But¦167794 he told her to bring her son¦167796 to him, and taking the boy from¦167798 her arms, he took¦167797 the body upstairs¦167802 to the room¦167802 he was¦167806 staying¦167806 in\add*, and laid him down on¦167809 his¦167811 bed¦167811.
\v 20 Then¦167813 he¦167813 called¦167813 out to Yahweh, “Yahweh, my¦167819 god¦167819, \add ≈would you¦167829 really bring tragedy to this widow¦167823 that I'm¦167826 staying¦167827 with¦167828 by¦167830 causing her¦167833 son¦167833 to die\add*?”
\v 21 Then¦167835 three¦167839 times¦167840 he¦167835 stretched¦167835 himself¦167835 over¦167836 the¦167838 boy's body¦167856 and¦167835 \add ≈begged\add* Yahweh, “Yahweh, my¦167847 god¦167847, please¦167849 let¦167848 this¦167853 child's¦167838 life¦167850 return¦167848 into his¦167856 \add ≈organs\add*.”\x + \xo 17:21: \xt 2Ki 4:34-35.\x*
\v 22 Yahweh¦167859 \add ≈took notice\add* of¦167860 Eliyah¦167861 and the \add ≈boy's life¦167863 returned¦167862 and he¦167869 revived\add*.
\p
\v 23 Then¦167871 Eliyah¦167872 \add ≈carried the boy back downstairs\add* and gave¦167881 him to his¦167882 mother¦167882 and \add ≈told her\add*, “Look¦167884, your¦167887 son's¦167887 \add ≈alive¦167886\add*.”
\p
\v 24 “Now¦167894 I¦167896 \add certainly\add* know¦167896 that you're a man¦167898 of¦167898 God¦167899,” the woman¦167890 responded¦167889, “And¦167893 \add ≈when you say¦167889 that you're speaking for Yahweh¦167903, it's really true\add*.”
\c 18
\s1 Eliyah versus Baal's prophets
\rem /s1 Elijah and the Prophets of Baal; Elijah and Obadiah; Elijah's Message to Ahab; The Contest on Mount Carmel
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈In the third¦167919 year¦167918 of drought, Yahweh¦167913 told Eliyah¦167917 to go¦167921 and show himself to King Ahav¦167925 and tell him that it would soon\add* rain¦167927,
\v 2 \add ≈so he¦167933 went¦167933 to present¦167935 himself¦167935\add* to Ahav¦167938.
\p \add Meanwhile\add* in¦167941 Shomron¦167941 \add !(Samaria¦167941)\add*, the¦167939 food shortage was¦167940 terrible
\v 3 and¦167952 \add King\add* Ahav¦167944 had summoned his palace¦167951 manager Ovadyah. (Ovadyah \add ≈was a sincere follower of\add* Yahweh¦167957.
\v 4 \add ≈When¦167960\add* \add Queen\add* Izevel¦167962 \add ≈had tried to kill\add* Yahweh's¦167965 prophets, Ovadyah¦167967 had \add ≈hidden¦167970\add* a hundred¦167968 prophets—fifty¦167971 \add ≈in¦167961 each of two caves\add* and \add ≈kept them supplied¦167974 with¦167961 food¦167975\add* and water¦167976.)
\v 5 \add King\add* Ahav¦167979 told Ovadyah¦167982, “\add We'll\add* go¦167983 \add ≈across the country\add* to¦167985 all the springs¦167989 and all the \add ≈valleys¦167994 that water¦167990 sometimes flows in\add*. Perhaps¦167995 we'll¦167997 find¦167997 \add some\add* grass¦167998 \add ≈so\add* we can keep¦167999 a horse¦168000 or a mule¦168001 \add or two\add* alive¦167999 and not¦168002 \add ≈lose our breeding stock\add*.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦168008\add* they divided¦168006 the¦168010 country \add into two\add*, and¦168006 \add ≈they each went off in¦168013 a different direction\add*.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈While\add* Ovadyah was¦168026 on¦168028 a path¦168028, Eliyah \add came to\add* meet¦168031 him. \add @Ovadyah\add* recognised¦168032 him and fell¦168033 \add ≈to his knees with¦168028 his face¦168036 to the ground, and asked\add*, “Is it \add really\add* you¦168038, my¦168040 master¦168040 Eliyah?”
\p
\v 8 “\add Yes,\add* it's¦168045 me,” he¦168043 \add ≈replied\add*. “\add Now\add* go¦168046 \add and\add* tell your¦168048 master¦168048 \add ≈that I'm here\add*.”
\p
\v 9 “How have¦168054 I¦168054 sinned¦168054,” Ovadyah \add ≈responded¦168052\add*, “that you're¦168057 giving¦168058 your¦168061 servant¦168061 \add ≈a death¦168065 sentence\add*?
\v 10 As¦168069 your¦168070 god¦168070 Yahweh¦168081 \add ≈lives\add*, my master¦168081 sent¦168080 \add ≈people to every kingdom to try to find¦168095 you, and if they¦168084 said¦168084 you weren't there, then he made¦168086 them promise under oath that it¦168095 was true\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦168097\add* now¦168097 you tell me to¦168102 tell my master¦168102 that \add *you're¦168098\add* here,
\v 12 \add ≈but¦168106\add* as soon as I leave you, Yahweh's¦168112 spirit¦168111 will¦168114 take you to \add ≈goodness knows¦168119 where¦168116\add*. \add ≈Meanwhile\add* I'll¦168109 go¦168109 and tell Ahav¦168122, and he'll come¦168120 here and not¦168123 find¦168124 you, \add ≈so\add* then¦168106 he'll kill¦168125 me¦168125, \add ≈even though I've been trying to obey Yahweh since¦168131 I was young\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈Haven't you heard\add*, my¦168136 master¦168136, what I did¦168140 when¦168141 Izevel¦168142 was killing¦168141 Yahweh's¦168145 prophets¦168144 and I hid¦168146 a hundred¦168149 of¦168148 them in¦168141 \add ≈two caves and kept them supplied¦168155 with¦168141 food¦168156\add* and water¦168157?
\v 14 \add ≈Yet¦168166\add* now¦168159 \add ≈you're¦168160 trying to¦168164 get me¦168167 killed¦168167 by telling my master¦168164 that he'll¦168167 find you\add* here.”
\p
\v 15 “As \add ≈Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦168173 lives—the one I serve\add*,” Eliyah¦168171 \add ≈replied\add*, “\add ≈I'll¦168180 definitely be here to¦168181 see him¦168177\add* today.”
\rem /s1 Elijah on Mount Carmel
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦168183\add* Ovadyah¦168184 went¦168183 \add and\add* informed Ahav¦168186 \add ≈who then¦168183 came\add* to meet¦168192 Eliyah¦168193.
