\p Ben¦169891-Hadad ran into the¦169881 city and¦169875 \add ≈hid in¦169900 an inner room\add*,
\v 31 \add ≈but¦169903\add* his servants¦169905 told him, “Listen, we've¦169909 heard¦169909 that¦169910 the¦169911 \add ≈Israeli¦169912 kings show\add* mercy. Please¦169920 let¦169919 us¦169919 wrap sackcloth¦169921 around our waists¦169922 and¦169923 go¦169925 out¦169925 to¦169926 Yisrael's¦169913 king¦169928 with¦169922 ropes¦169923 on¦169922 our heads¦169924—perhaps¦169930 he'll¦169931 \add ≈spare\add* your¦169934 life¦169934.”
\v 32 \add ≈So¦169936\add* they¦169936 wrapped their waists¦169938 in¦169938 sacking and put ropes¦169939 on¦169938 their heads¦169940, and went¦169941 to Yisrael's¦169945 king¦169944, saying¦169946, “Your¦169947 servant¦169947 Ben¦169948-Hadad¦169950 \add ≈asks you to spare his\add* life¦169955.”
