\v 41 Then¦170134 he quickly¦170134 \add ≈uncovered\add* his¦170141 eyes¦170141 and¦170134 the king¦170144 recognised¦170142 that¦170146 he was¦170147 one¦170147 of¦170147 the prophets¦170147,
\v 42 and \add @the prophet\add* told him, “Yahweh¦170154 says¦170153 that because¦170155 you¦170156 \add ≈released\add* a man¦170159 \add ≈who should¦170156 have¦170156 been executed\add*, then¦170150 your life¦170164 \add will be required\add* in place of his, and your people in place of his people.”
