\v 8 \add ≈So¦170372\add* she wrote¦170372 letters¦170373 in¦170377 Ahav's¦170375 name¦170374 and sealed¦170376 them with¦170377 his¦170377 seal¦170377. Then¦170372 she sent¦170378 them to¦170381 the¦170383 city¦170389 elders¦170383 and nobles¦170387 who lived¦170390 near Navot¦170393.
\v 9 \add ≈This is what\add* she¦170395 wrote¦170395, “Announce a fast¦170400, and¦170401 seat¦170401 Navot¦170404 hear the head¦170405 \add ≈of¦170405 the table\add*.
\v 10 Then seat¦170408 two¦170409 \add ≈troublemakers opposite¦170414\add* him, and get them¦170415 to testify¦170415 against¦170415 him that he cursed God¦170418 and the¦170419 king¦170419. Then take¦170420 him outside and \add ≈pelt him with rocks¦170421 until he's¦170422 dead\add*.
\p
\v 11 Then¦170424 the elders¦170427 and¦170424 nobles¦170428 of the city¦170431 did what Izevel¦170435 had instructed them via the letters¦170438:
\v 12 They¦170445 announced a fast¦170444 and¦170445 seated¦170445 Navot¦170448 near the head¦170449 \add ≈of¦170449 the table\add*,
\v 13 then¦170452 two¦170453 worthless¦170457 men¦170454 \add ≈were seated opposite¦170459 him\add*, and they¦170460 testified¦170460 in¦170477 front¦170459 of \add all\add* the people¦170467 that Navot had cursed God¦170471 and the king¦170472. \add ≈So¦170452\add* Navot was led out¦170473 of the city¦170475 and \add ≈killed by having rocks¦170477 thrown at¦170477 him\add*,
\v 14 and¦170487 they¦170480 sent¦170480 \add a message\add* to Izevel¦170483 \add ≈to tell her that Navot¦170486 had¦170485 been¦170485 stoned¦170485 to death\add*.
\p
\v 15 As soon as Izevel¦170491 heard¦170490 that Navot had¦170494 been¦170494 \add ≈executed\add*, \add *she\add* told Ahav¦170501, “\add ≈Go on¦170515 now\add* \add and\add* \add ≈take¦170503 over\add* Navot's¦170495 vineyard¦170506 that he refused¦170511 to¦170499 \add ≈sell\add* you, because¦170492 he's \add ≈not¦170517 around any more\add*—he's dead.”
\v 16 As soon as Ahav¦170526 heard¦170525 that¦170527 Navot¦170529 was dead, \add *he\add* went¦170532 to the vineyard¦170535 to take¦170538 possession¦170538 of¦170538 it¦170538.
\rem /s1 Elijah Pronounces God's Sentence
