\p
\v 20 \add When Eliyah arrived\add*, Ahav¦170603 \add ≈asked\add* \add *him\add*, “\add Ah,\add* my enemy¦170608. Have¦170607 you¦170612 found¦170607 me¦170607?”
\p “\add Yes,\add* I've¦170610 found \add >you\add*,” \add @Eliyah\add* \add ≈replied\add*. “\add ≈It seems you've¦170612 sold¦170612 your soul by doing¦170613 what Yahweh's¦170616 finds to be evil¦170614\add*.
\v 21 \add Yahweh says that\add* \add ≈he's about¦170619 to send disaster on¦170628 you to destroy\add* you and \add ≈every male in¦170628 your household—whether they're slaves or free\add*.
