\p
\v 27 As soon as Ahav¦170719 heard¦170718 that message¦170722, he tore¦170724 his clothes¦170725 and dressed in sacking and fasted¦170732. He \add even\add* slept in the sackcloth¦170728, and he walked around \add ≈slowly\add* \add with his head down\add*.
\p
\v 28 Then Yahweh¦170742 \add ≈asked\add* Eliyah¦170745 (from Tishbe¦170746),
\v 29 “Have you¦170749 \add ≈noticed\add* that Ahav¦170753 has¦170752 \add ≈shown repentance towards me¦170754\add*? Because he's humbled¦170758 himself¦170758, I won't¦170760 bring¦170762 \add ≈that disaster on¦170765 his family while he's still alive\add*, \add but rather\add* I'll¦170762 do \add *it\add* \add ≈during his son's¦170767 reign\add*.”
\c 22
\s1 prophet Mikayehu and King Ahav
\rem /s1 Joint Campaign with Judah against Aram; Jehoshaphat and Ahab; Micaiah Prophesies Against Ahab; The Prophet Micaiah Warns Ahab
\s4 Both kingdoms
