\p
\v 13 \add ≈Meanwhile\add* the messenger¦171009 who¦171010 had¦171012 gone¦171012 to call¦171014 Mikayehu¦171015 told him¦171017, “Listen, please¦171021, \add ≈all the other prophets¦171023 agree together as they prophesy victory for\add* the king¦171030. Please¦171033 let¦171031 your¦171034 message¦171034 be \add ≈similar to theirs\add* and¦171039 \add ≈be positive\add*.”
\p
\v 14 “As surely as Yahweh lives,” Mikayehu¦171043 \add ≈responded¦171042\add*, “I'll¦171055 only tell Ahav what Yahweh tells¦171051 me to say¦171051.”
\p
\v 15 \add ≈When¦171057\add* he¦171057 got to¦171058 King¦171060 \add Ahav\add*, the king¦171081 asked him¦171063, “Mikayehu¦171064, should we¦171065 \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦171068-Gilead¦171069, or \add ≈not\add*?”
\p “Go \add ≈ahead\add* and be successful¦171077,” he \add ≈replied\add*, “and Yahweh¦171079 will give¦171078 \add ≈it back to\add* the king.”
\p
